<Page title="About — Alexander Campos" description="Alex Campos, Virginia. Bank operations, independent software, music, and a French bulldog named Oliver.">
  <article>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Alex. I’m 26 and live in Virginia.</p>
    <p>
      I work in bank operations and build software outside it. Some is practical,
      like <a href="/projects/reframed">a resume tool</a>. Some starts with a
      question I can’t leave alone, like how an assistant should remember things
      without quietly deciding who I am.
    </p>

    <figure class="office-photo">
      <img src="/images/office.jpg" alt="Oliver, a grey French bulldog, sitting at my laptop" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <figcaption>Oliver, helping.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      The word I keep coming back to is sovereignty. Having a say in the systems
      I depend on, and enough room to make a different choice when things change.
      It connects my interests in AI, finance, geopolitics, security, and business.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reduction is how I tend to think. What is the actual constraint? Who can
      change it? Who pays? I like getting a complicated situation down to the
      few things that determine what can happen, then doing something with it.
    </p>
    <p>
      I use cloud models and care about running my own tools. I work inside a
      large institution and like building things myself. I’m comfortable with
      those tensions; I don’t have a neat theory that makes all of it fit.
    </p>
    <p>
      The personal ambition is enough ownership, competence, and financial
      independence to have meaningful control over my life, without giving up
      the principles that make that freedom worth having.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some things just don’t need a business case. The music, the desk on this
      site, Oliver. I want room for those too.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      The code is on <a href="https://github.com/notaprompt">GitHub</a>.
      My background is on <a href="/resume">the resume</a> and
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexander-d-campos/">LinkedIn</a>.
      There’s a <a href="/influences">bookshelf</a>, too.
    </p>
    <p><a href="mailto:alex@campos.works">alex@campos.works</a></p>
  </article>
</Page>

